            <provenance type="observed" subtype="" xml:lang="en">
              <p>It is not known whether E. Kosev discovered the seal or he was simply the one who presented it to the museum. In the Corpus of 2009 and the Museum Catalogue of 2011, Jordanov writes that the seal “was passed on to the Archaeological Museum by E. Kosev in 1984”, but in Jordanov, 2006, 353, the author says that the seal with inventory number 251 was purchased by that person in 1994.</p>
